WEBVTT

00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:14.200
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> This is a choir.

00:00:16.914 --> 00:00:19.826
They're called the Oxford Gargoyles.

00:00:22.524 --> 00:00:25.430
A gargoyle is a type of statue.

00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:31.361
You see them on a lot of old buildings in Oxford and other cities.

00:00:34.446 --> 00:00:38.273
Today the Oxford Gargoyles have a rehearsal.

00:00:39.607 --> 00:00:42.073
They have a new song to practise,

00:00:43.006 --> 00:00:47.400
an old English folk song called <i>Scarborough Fair</i>.

00:00:49.764 --> 00:00:53.267
Let’s find out more about the choir and the people in it.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.315
How many people are in the choir?

00:00:58.208 --> 00:01:00.032
<v><b>Freddie:</b></v> There are thirteen people in the choir.

00:01:00.398 --> 00:01:01.944
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Are you all students?

00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:04.608
<v><b>Steph:</b></v> Yes, we’re all students at Oxford University.

00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:05.928
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you study?

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.376
<v><b>Steph:</b></v> I study music.

00:01:07.576 --> 00:01:08.536
<v><b>Alex:</b></v> I study music.

00:01:09.176 --> 00:01:10.209
<v><b>Tegan:</b></v> I study music.

00:01:10.449 --> 00:01:13.879
<v><b>Nell:</b></v> I study languages, specifically French and Italian.

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:16.811
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you practise?

00:01:17.691 --> 00:01:21.772
<v><b>Nell:</b></v> We practise twice a week – on Wednesdays and Saturdays.

00:01:21.812 --> 00:01:23.845
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How long do you practise for?

00:01:24.185 --> 00:01:26.193
<v><b>Steph:</b></v> Each rehearsal is three hours long.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.865
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you give concerts?

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:31.812
<v><b>Tegan:</b></v> We usually give concerts once a month.

00:01:32.147 --> 00:01:34.028
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where do you give concerts?

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.880
<v><b>Nell:</b></v> We give concerts in lots of different locations.

00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:43.336
We give concerts in bars and in theatres and in churches.

00:01:43.663 --> 00:01:46.475
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of music do you like singing?

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:51.035
<v><b>Steph:</b></v> I like singing lots of different types of music, especially jazz and opera.

00:01:51.262 --> 00:01:53.810
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you think everybody can sing?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.738
<v><b>Freddie:</b></v> I think everyone can sing because everyone can talk.

00:01:59.671 --> 00:02:01.681
<v><b>Tegan:</b></v> I think everybody can learn how to sing.

00:02:01.961 --> 00:02:05.344
<v><b>Alex:</b></v> I think everyone apart from my dad can sing. Yes.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.631
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Why do you like singing?

00:02:08.655 --> 00:02:09.728
<v><b>Freddie:</b></v> I love music

00:02:09.835 --> 00:02:17.108
and I love being able to make music with my own body, my own voice,

00:02:17.255 --> 00:02:19.563
without needing any extra tools.

00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:25.150
<v><b>Nell:</b></v> I enjoy singing a lot because I think it’s a really fun thing to do.

00:02:25.517 --> 00:02:27.880
And it’s also a very social activity,

00:02:27.938 --> 00:02:30.861
so you can do it with anyone, with any of your friends,

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.694
and you can do it at any time, or in any place.

00:02:34.302 --> 00:02:37.257
<v><b>Steph:</b></v> I like singing because I feel happy when I sing.

00:02:38.043 --> 00:02:41.730
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you prefer singing solo or with a group?

00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:46.640
<v><b>Tegan:</b></v> I definitely prefer singing in a group because I like singing with my friends

00:02:46.641 --> 00:02:49.117
and I think it’s really fun to be able to sing together.

00:02:50.137 --> 00:02:52.992
<v><b>Alex:</b></v> It’s nice to sing solos, but it is more pressure as well.

00:02:53.485 --> 00:02:56.498
<v><b>Steph:</b></v> I like both solo singing and choir singing.

00:03:01.385 --> 00:03:06.737
<v><b>Choir:</b></v> <i>Are you going to Scarborough Fair</i>?

00:03:08.703 --> 00:03:14.191
<i>Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme </i>

00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:23.560
<i>Remember me to one who lives there </i>

00:03:24.984 --> 00:03:30.601
<i>She once was a true love of mine. </i>

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:46.040
<i>Tell her to make me a cambric shirt </i>

00:03:47.082 --> 00:03:57.095
<i>Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme. </i>

00:03:58.035 --> 00:04:07.256
<i>Without no seams nor needle work </i>

00:04:10.026 --> 00:04:20.340
<i>Then she'll be a true love of mine. </i>